  [PASS] [data] S2b the degeneracy is steep: kappa moves by more than 0.15 between Upsilon_disc = 0.5 and 0.7   (0.636 -> 0.434)
  [PASS] [identity] S2d the shape-only estimator is immune to a common distance rescaling (< 1e-5): the free offset absorbs it by construction   (8.4e-11)
  [PASS] [data] S2d2 while the standard fit is not: a 10 per cent common rescaling moves it by more than 15 per cent   (22.4%)
  [PASS] [data] S2e the replication agrees with the repository's estimator B at Upsilon_bul = 0.7, Upsilon_disc = 0.5 and 0.7 (0.529, 0.574) within 0.01   (0.528, 0.573)
  [PASS] [data] S2f AGAINST THE EARLIER ERROR BAR: the bulge mass-to-light ratio moves estimator B by more than twice the 0.043 previously quoted   (bulge term 0.114; total 0.175)
  [PASS] [data] S2g the deep band (g_bar < 0.1 a0, quality-cut, error-weighted) gives kappa between 0.40 and 0.60 for Upsilon_disc 0.5-0.7   (0.558, 0.492, 0.441)
  [PASS] [data] S2h AGAINST INTEREST: giving every deep point equal weight (no quality cut) lowers kappa by at least 0.05 at every Upsilon   (0.444, 0.388, 0.342)
  [PASS] [injection] I1 the standard fit returns the injected a0 to 2 per cent at 0.7, 1.0 and 1.3 x canonical   (1.004, 1.008, 0.998)
  [PASS] [injection] I2 the shape-only estimator returns the injected a0 to 3 per cent through a 0.08 dex common offset that biases the standard fit by > 15 per cent   (shape 1.023, 1.015, 1.004; standard 1.662, 1.639, 1.603)
  [PASS] [injection] I3 the deep-band fit returns the injected a0 to 5 per cent   (1.001, 1.021, 1.008)
