  check of the gmax route against the closed law: ratio 2.1264 vs E^(4/3) c^2/f(c) ratio 2.1264
  20:1 rule: two point hypotheses Delta apart, Gaussian error sigma: expected ln B = Delta^2/(2 sigma^2) >= ln 20  =>  sigma <= Delta/sqrt(2 ln 20) = Delta/2.448
     constant vs halo-emergent at z = 2.5: Delta = 0.328 -> sigma <= 0.134 dex;   constant vs H(z): Delta = 0.576 -> sigma <= 0.235 dex
  error amplification of the kernel inversion  a0 = g_bar/y,  nu(y) = g_obs/g_bar :
     d ln a0 = (1 + 1/n) d ln g_bar - (1/n) d ln g_obs,   n = d ln nu/d ln y
